="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I432863d5edfdb729e700a39cacd5d9fc7874f26f" commit="981d000ceaaed8afd22b3d3ea0344ef7ed57c84c" commit_message="authpolicy: Added authpolicyd boilerplate code  BUG=chromium:653509 TEST=emerges. Ad hoc test at runtime with future commits. CQ-DEPEND=CL:394589  Change-Id: I432863d5edfdb729e700a39cacd5d9fc7874f26f Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/394646 Commit-Ready: Roman Sorokin &lt;rsorokin@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Roman Sorokin &lt;rsorokin@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Zentaro Kavanagh &lt;zentaro@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Roman Sorokin &lt;rsorokin@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Mike Frysinger &lt;vapier@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="394646" owner_email="rsorokin@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="5" project="chromiumos/platform2" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform2" ref="refs/changes/46/394646/5" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I4d9868c0dcbf3e56cdae79bd455c8dc067fc1542" commit="f462db52094a4dceb1f1b2d31d3040e9b0814a78" commit_message="cryptohome: set system salt for attestationd at start  For TPM2 systems, send system salt to attestationd using SetSystemSalt message, since attestationd doesn't have privileges to read it itself.  CQ-DEPEND=CL:395107 BUG=chrome-os-partner:54712 TEST=unit tests, check that there are no &quot;Could not get size of      system salt&quot; messages for TpmAttestationDoesKeyExist  Change-Id: I4d9868c0dcbf3e56cdae79bd455c8dc067fc1542 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/395166 Commit-Ready: Andrey Pronin &lt;apronin@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Andrey Pronin &lt;apronin@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Darren Krahn &lt;dkrahn@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="3" gerrit_number="395166" owner_email="apronin@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/platform2" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform2" ref="refs/changes/66/395166/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="3"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I5a9c9ee446bdd004e532e2bf3f8b2ffa2b7b46b3" commit="85a073c0fb331866783202f69deaa41adcde925b" commit_message="goofy: change run_if behavior  For a FactoryTest, if run_if argument is set to 'foo.bar', then Goofy will skip the test if 'foo.bar' is set to False in shopfloor aux data.  If 'foo.bar' is not set, then Goofy would *not* skip the test.  However, in current usage, this behavior is annoying.  For example:    FactoryTest(       ...       run_if='device_data.component.HAS_LTE',       ...)  This test will not be run if and only if 'HAS_LTE' is set, and is set to False.  And in most of projects, they want the test to be skipped if the value is not set.  In this CL, if key is not found in aux data, the query result is considered None (or False).  Therefore, in the same situation above, when HAS_LTE is not set, the test will be skipped.  Another use case for run_if is:    FactoryTest(       ...       run_if='!device_data.complete_smt',       ...)  If complete_smt is not set, the test *will* still be run in new implementation.  BUG=b:31678190 TEST=make test  Change-Id: I5a9c9ee446bdd004e532e2bf3f8b2ffa2b7b46b3 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/394511 Commit-Ready: Wei-Han Chen &lt;stimim@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Wei-Han Chen &lt;stimim@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Shun-Hsing Ou &lt;shunhsingou@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="394511" owner_email="stimim@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/platform/factory" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/factory" ref="refs/changes/11/394511/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I2f9ea682f6edfe787f4e55f22a44f35c39e36f39" commit="da328798937e12c77e557e724b8f57f02799f32b" commit_message="hardware_EC: don't run on devices without Google EC.  BUG=chromium:655441 TEST=h